{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "0F22", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{F}, \\mathcal{F}_0, \\alpha)$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\mathcal{L}, \\mathcal{L}_0, \\lambda)$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\mathbf{Z} \\longrightarrow \\mathbf{Z},\\quad\nn \\longmapsto\n\\chi((\\mathcal{F}, \\mathcal{F}_0, \\alpha) \\otimes\n(\\mathcal{L}, \\mathcal{L}_0, \\lambda)^{\\otimes n})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\leq \\dim(\\text{Supp}(\\mathcal{F}))$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{proposition-hilbert-triple}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c36aff888ebdd1bd46303108eeba41a523aded42bedc1c2961e88687b9bb779d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cb81947f9d82e39b7646cf5163b8df910285add39242bf50f7264f09225ceeee", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a coherent triple.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an invertible coherent\ntriple. Then the function\n<MATH_0003>\nis a polynomial of degree <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2c5668acdd9f9185c4e031209fb0238fb787a338edc1b76410641440c3a2b9c0", "unit_id": "tag:0F27:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraization", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0F22", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F} = 0$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$1$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$X$", "MATH_0009": "$2$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:26dbaedbc66c85a513b24be08112878d12edd05e779d085f6b2e296736e3e2bf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8aab4e237673c2ef8789b18af61c81e842a2cc100936ca47c931d65cffca3f1b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nMore precisely, if <MATH_0001>, then the function is constant.\nIf <MATH_0002> has finite support in <MATH_0003>, then the function is constant.\nIf the support of <MATH_0004> in <MATH_0005> has dimension <MATH_0006>, i.e., the\nclosure of the support of <MATH_0007> in <MATH_0008> has dimension <MATH_0009>, then\nthe function is linear, etc.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4f3865e6cb428def73deb170949c0dd873d06822081c427ce533c82c232bcb3d", "unit_id": "tag:0F22:prose-0003"}
